  "notes": "{汚|よご}れる is an intransitive ichidan verb meaning 'to become dirty' or 'to get stained.'\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{汚|よご}す→汚す：02327_yogosu⟧ (transitive, to make dirty)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{汚|よご}れている describes the resultant state of being dirty, not the process.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{服|ふく}→服：00695_fuku⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{汚|よご}れる: clothes get dirty\n- ⟦{手|て}→手：00569_te⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{汚|よご}れている: hands are dirty\n- ⟦{泥|どろ}→泥：03492_doro⟧⟦で→で：00502_de⟧{汚|よご}れる: to get dirty with mud\n- ⟦{白|しろ}い→白い：00587_shiroi⟧⟦もの→物：02259_mono⟧⟦は→は：00079_ha⟧{汚|よご}れやすい: white things get dirty easily\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{汚|よご}れ→汚れ：03186_yogore⟧ (noun): dirt, stain\n- ⟦{汚|きたな}い→汚い：00788_kitanai⟧ (adjective): dirty, filthy\n- ⟦{清潔|せいけつ}→清潔：01583_seiketsu⟧ (noun/na-adj): clean, hygienic",
